  "question": {
    "text": "Combustion of glucose \\(\\left(\\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_{12} \\mathrm{O}_6\\right)\\) produces \\(\\mathrm{CO}_2\\) and water. The amount of oxygen (in g) required for the complete combustion of \\(900 \\mathrm{~g}\\) of glucose is :\n[Molar mass of glucose in \\(\\mathrm{g} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}=180\\) ]"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "480",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "800",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "960",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "32",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{C}_6 \\mathrm{H}_{12} \\mathrm{O}_{6(\\mathrm{~s})}+6 \\mathrm{O}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})} \\longrightarrow 6 \\mathrm{CO}_{2(\\mathrm{~g})}+6 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}_{(\\theta)} \\\\ & \\frac{900}{180} \\\\ & =5 \\mathrm{~mol} \\quad 30 \\mathrm{~mol}\\end{aligned}$\nMass of $\\mathrm{O}_2$ required $=30 \\times 32=960 \\mathrm{gm}$"
  }
